            <ArticleTitle>Swallowing a Surgeon: Toward Clinical Nanorobots.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>492-497</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.accounts.6b00495</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this Account, &quot;a step toward clinical nanorobots&quot; is proposed as one of the Holy Grails in chemistry, which could lead to a great leap in the field of biomedicines when accomplished. We review our preliminary contributions to this challenge by engineering chaperonin protein GroEL to generate de novo structures and functions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
